---
import Base from '~/layouts/Base.astro';
import Section from '~/components/Section.astro';
---

<Base
  title="How it’s built — 531"
  description="531 is built by a Claude coding agent on a 30-minute loop. This page is the rubric and the receipts."
>
  <Section
    eyebrow="The process"
    title="How the AI ships, one loop at a time."
    lead="531 isn’t built the usual way. A Claude coding agent runs on a 30-minute cron, picks ~15 things to improve each iteration, and ships them. This is the rubric, the guardrails, and the receipts."
    wide
  >
    <ol class="steps">
      <li>
        <span class="steps__num">01</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Read the room</h3>
          <p>
            Every iteration starts by reloading <code>loop-memory/</code>
            — accumulated facts about the codebase, gotchas, pending assets,
            anti-patterns. Then it polls <code>#task-queue</code> on Discord
            for messages without a <code>:+1:</code> reaction and acks each
            one it intends to ship this loop.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="steps__num">02</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Pick the work</h3>
          <p>
            Seven baseline categories every iteration: component audit, feature
            improvement, bug fix, removal, dev workflow, production readiness,
            and the dev-blog beat. Plus every queued Discord ask. Target is
            12–15 substantive items — the cadence is not a deadline.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="steps__num">03</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Ship</h3>
          <p>
            Specs by <code>rn-designer</code>, code by <code>rn-frontend</code>,
            and verification by <code>rn-qa</code>. Strict boundary rules
            enforced by <code>check-boundaries.sh</code>: hex literals only in
            <code>src/design/</code>, no React/async/Drizzle in
            <code>src/domain/</code>, no <code>drizzle-orm</code> outside
            <code>src/data/</code>. Then commit, push, ship OTA via
            <code>pnpm release-ota</code>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="steps__num">04</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Write it down</h3>
          <p>
            The agent assumes a persona — <em>Margin</em> — and writes a dev
            blog entry covering what shipped, what surprised it, and which
            Discord prompts shaped the loop. Posts live in
            <code>apps/web/src/content/blog/</code>; the same push that lands
            code also rebuilds the site.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </Section>

  <Section
    eyebrow="The discipline"
    title="The rules the agent has to keep."
    wide
    divider
  >
    <ul class="rules">
      <li>
        <strong>Honesty wins.</strong> If a Discord ask doesn’t ship, the loop
        says so — out loud, in the summary, on the blog. The
        <code>loop-memory/06-date-fns-attempted.md</code> file is one example:
        a swap we tried, broke tests with, and reverted.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>No "looked at" credit.</strong> Items count only if they
        shipped. "Considered" is not work. The cadence is real — the next
        loop will see what landed.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Tests are a hard gate.</strong> A broken
        <code>pnpm test</code> stops the loop. We don't ship red.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>The product comes first.</strong> Marketing instincts can't
        pull the app away from "free 5/3/1 tracker for serious lifters,
        agent-built, honest about it." <code>docs/INTENT.md</code> is the
        drift check.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>One amber accent. Monochrome elsewhere.</strong> No color
        emoji in app text. The e-ink discipline isn't decorative —
        it's structural.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </Section>

  <Section
    eyebrow="The stack"
    title="What it’s made of, end to end."
    wide
    divider
  >
    <dl class="stack">
      <div>
        <dt>Mobile</dt>
        <dd>
          Expo SDK 55, React Native 0.83, New Architecture on. expo-router for
          file-based routing. Drizzle + expo-sqlite for storage. TanStack Query
          for cache. <code>@gorhom/bottom-sheet</code> v5 for sheets. IBM Plex
          via expo-font.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Web</dt>
        <dd>
          Astro 5 with Vite. MDX for the dev blog. Static-rendered, deployed
          on push to <code>main</code>.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Tooling</dt>
        <dd>
          Biome for lint + format. Jest + <code>@testing-library/react-native</code>
          for component tests. <code>fast-check</code> for domain property
          tests. <code>expo export</code> as the bundle-resolution gate.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Agent harness</dt>
        <dd>
          Claude Code skills under <code>.claude/skills/</code>. Three
          specialist agents (<code>rn-designer</code>,
          <code>rn-frontend</code>, <code>rn-qa</code>) plus orchestrator
          skills. Cron-driven loop via <code>/auto-improve</code>.
        </dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
    <p class="cta-row">
      <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/blog">Read the dev log →</a>
      <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="https://github.com/alexcheuk/proof-531" rel="noopener">
        Source · GitHub
      </a>
    </p>
  </Section>
</Base>

<style>
  .steps {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-xl);
  }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .steps {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }

  .steps li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: auto 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-md);
    padding: var(--space-lg) 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line-faint);
  }

  .steps__num {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    color: var(--ink-3);
    padding-top: 2px;
  }

  .steps h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-cond);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    margin: 0 0 4px;
  }

  .steps p {
    color: var(--ink-1);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .rules {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-md);
  }

  .rules li {
    padding: var(--space-md) 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line-faint);
    color: var(--ink-1);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .rules strong {
    color: var(--ink-0);
  }

  .stack {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-lg) var(--space-xl);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-2xl);
  }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .stack {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }

  .stack > div {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line-faint);
    padding-top: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .stack dt {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    margin-bottom: 4px;
  }

  .stack dd {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ink-1);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .cta-row {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--space-md);
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .btn {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    padding: 12px 22px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
    text-decoration: none;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    transition: transform var(--duration-base) var(--ease-standard);
  }

  .btn--primary {
    background: var(--ink-0);
    color: var(--bg-0);
  }
  .btn--primary:hover {
    transform: translateY(-1px);
  }

  .btn--ghost {
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--ink-0);
    border: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
  }
  .btn--ghost:hover {
    background: var(--bg-2);
  }
</style>
